From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium: disable internal audio

This device is a dedicated bit-perfect player feeding a USB DAC (Chord
Mojo 2), which is a separate ALSA card on the USB bus. The on-board audio
path is never used, so disable it to free the SLIMbus clock/IRQ domain and
stop the idle WCD9340 codec from sitting on the SoC:

  - &sound    : the on-board ASoC machine card
  - &wcd9340  : the WCD9340 codec (SLIMbus device)
  - &slim     : the SLIMbus NGD controller (audio-only on SDM845)
  - &slimbam  : the SLIMbus BAM DMA controller

Nothing on beryllium uses SLIMbus except the codec, so this is safe and
fully reversible (reflash a kernel without the patch to restore internal
audio). The hunk appends overrides at the end of the shared -common.dtsi,
so it covers both the EBBG and Tianma panel variants; it locates by the
trailing &q6voicedai block, so the line number is approximate.

Signed-off-by: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
@@ -936,3 +936,9 @@
 		reg = <VOICEMMODE1>;
 	};
 };
+
+/* Dedicated USB-DAC appliance: free SLIMbus + the internal codec (audio is USB-only). */
+&sound { status = "disabled"; };
+&wcd9340 { status = "disabled"; };
+&slim { status = "disabled"; };
+&slimbam { status = "disabled"; };
--
2.51.0
